An alias is a verb of your own that turns into something else when
you press enter.

  alias                      lists the ones you have.
  alias <name> <command>     creates it, or changes it.
  unalias <name>             deletes it.

Inside the command you can leave gaps for whatever you type after
the alias:

  $*$              everything you wrote after it.
  $1$              the first word, $2$ the second, and so on.
  $arg1:something$ the first word, or 'something' if you gave none.

And a semicolon chains several commands into one:

  alias greet say hello;smile

A whole example: "alias g say hello $1$" makes "g Guardia" say
"hello Guardia".
